{"seq":1,"mint":"C27","verb":"claim","status":"ok","model":"openai/gpt-5.6-luna","approach":"split","literals":false,"findings":[{"kind":"contradicts","clause":"`search_key` stores world_root's own spelling as the key whenever the search root and the worktree root name the same directory","clause_quoted":true,"facts":["F6","F18","F21"],"quoted_from":"output","evidence":"fn search_key(root: &Path, world_root: &str) -> String {\n    let resolved = resolve_key(root);\n    if world_root.is_empty() {\n        return resolved;\n    }\n    let same = fs::canonicalize(root)\n        .ok()\n        .zip(fs::canonicalize(world_root).ok())\n        .map(|(a, b)| a == b)\n        .unwrap_or(false);\n    if same { world_root.to_string() } else { resolved }\n}","why":"If either canonicalization fails, `same` becomes false and the function returns `resolved`, not `world_root.to_string()`. Thus the claimed behavior does not hold for every pair of paths naming the same directory.","quoted":true}],"at":1790112784,"cost":0.02133074,"elapsed_ms":111772,"attempts":3,"not_verbatim":0,"literals_refuted":0,"not_a_quantity":0,"kind_off_verb":0,"refuted":0}
